-# What a save answers the form in the capture frame with. A save that went
-# through touches five places: the head, which counts the amounts up; the
-# frame, which holds the read-only list and the history again -- or the form
-# with the saved values where Speichern und weiter bearbeiten asks for it; the
-# bodies of the Abmelde-Formular and the receipt sections, since the saved
-# values decide whether the form may be made and what both documents say; and
-# the flash slot of the layout, which names what changed. Values the model
-# refused bring the form back alone, with its errors.
- if @dereg_saved
  = turbo_stream.replace("dereg-summary", partial: "summary")
  = turbo_stream.update("deregistration_capture", partial: @dereg_stay ? "capture_form" : "capture_body")
  = turbo_stream.update("dereg-form-body", partial: "deregistration_form")
  = turbo_stream.update("dereg-receipt-body", partial: "refund_receipt")
  = turbo_stream.update("flash", partial: "layouts/flash", collection: %i[notice warning alert], as: :level)
- else
  = turbo_stream.update("deregistration_capture", partial: "capture_form")
